{"c":[{"id":"bf2aa89d755a6e5f","sum":"SC1: request text is ModelText only (derived for reformats; casts outside src/privacy/ fail sc1-boundary); exclude.ts counts lower/upper/digit; excluded values read in as [withheld]. Every slot needs a shapes.ts row. Field-format mints trace to their window source.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"2925274083aef64a","sum":"SC1: exclude.ts high-entropy counts lower/upper/digit only (symbols broke B25 held-16); excluded values read in as [withheld]. Request text is ModelText only (own/t/descriptor/candidate/memoryText, derived for reformats); casts outside src/privacy/ fail sc1-boundary.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T200650Z-ffcd5d83b2f9fc55","text":"SC1 exclude.ts: the high-entropy rule counts only lower/upper/digit classes; counting symbols flagged corpus URL paths (51310/forms/greenhouse-apply) and broke B25 held-16. Excluded values become [withheld] at read-in; writes and memory refuse any text holding it.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T211138Z-929a7c53a65ffe04","text":"SC1: request text compiles only as ModelText (privacy/disclosure.ts own/t/descriptor/candidate/memoryText); mint a reformatted value with derived(base, text), which refuses words the screen never showed. A ModelText cast outside src/privacy/ fails test/sc1-boundary.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"6af8d35d2cbd1bc9","sum":"Field-format candidates carry fieldFormat provenance and assumptions through both verifier wordings; validation traces the mint to its window source. Every request slot needs a privacy/shapes.ts row, or verify throws OutOfShape; purpose-less requests carry own() only.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T213034Z-ef7ccd2a17aa97dd","text":"Field-format fill candidates carry fieldFormat provenance and conversion assumptions through both verifier wordings; planner validation traces a genuine mint to its original window source and rechecks provenance, since formatted text need not occur verbatim.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T215427Z-85a4a1e31491fed7","text":"Every request slot needs a row in helper/src/privacy/shapes.ts: Disclosure.verify throws OutOfShape for a path with no row, a mint reason the row disallows, or text over its max; a request with no purpose may carry only own() wording.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e5f9cbd94aab9fee","sum":"All app builds run privacy_gate.sh: accepted.ts needs pv2-sites-send + ha2-copied-conversation; Vercel dev opt-in refused; onboarding shows bundled PrivacyPromise.txt; release sets CARET_RELEASE_HOST=1. Disclosure keys match KEY (note_1); dynamic maps need a shapes.ts childGlob.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"009e4aa697218076","sum":"privacy_gate.sh runs on every build (Debug, build-app.sh, helper bundling): accepted.ts records pv2-sites-send and ha2-copied-conversation; CARET_DEV_VERCEL_GEMINI=1 refused; onboarding renders PrivacyPromise.txt; release sets CARET_RELEASE_HOST=1 (no Vercel).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T001204Z-bb38791614f982ff","text":"Caret app builds, including Debug, run scripts/privacy_gate.sh; helper/src/privacy/accepted.ts must record lead acceptance of pv2-sites-send and ha2-copied-conversation before builds pass, and CARET_DEV_VERCEL_GEMINI=1 is refused at build time.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T002947Z-c019705c5089f866","text":"The privacy gate also covers apps/caret/scripts/build-app.sh and direct helper bundling; onboarding must render generated Contents/Resources/PrivacyPromise.txt. Release child environments set CARET_RELEASE_HOST=1, which refuses every Vercel route even with a dev opt-in.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ceaba173a4e941d3","sum":"Xcode privacy phases: first checks source plists, last needs the processed bundle plist. Release env extraction keeps only TypeSafe settings. Disclosure.walk refuses body keys with spaces (use note_1); dynamic state maps need a childGlob rule in shapes.ts.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T004510Z-16ddc03f0a00f357","text":"Xcode's first privacy phase checks source plists; its last requires the processed bundle plist as an input. Release helper env-file extraction preserves TypeSafe key/provider/model/cap and refuses other providers before spawn.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T030901Z-9525a678a3afd6cf","text":"Disclosure.walk refuses any request-body key outside KEY (no spaces), so ids like 'note 1' cannot be state keys (INT1 uses note_1); a state map with dynamic keys also needs a childGlob rule in privacy/shapes.ts besides its .* row.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
